.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Thin cryptographic layer.
.PP
Every primitive (hash, random, ChaCha20, AES, Poly1305, GCM, X25519, ECDH, ML\-KEM, sntrup761, EdDSA, ECDSA, RSA) is delegated to libgcrypt. This module holds only the helpers the rest of the library needs around them: initialization, random bytes, constant\-time comparison, secret wiping and incremental hashing.  SSH\-specific constructions live in packet.h (the binary packet protocol), kex.h (key exchange and key derivation) and key.h (host and user keys).
.PP
There is deliberately no MD5 and no SHA\-1 here, and no HMAC: SSH integrity comes from AEAD ciphers only.
.PP
All functions return a gf_status.  Call gf_crypto_init once, before creating threads, or let the first use do it.
