.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
int \fBgf_crypto_init\fP (void);
Initialize libgcrypt if the application has not already done so. Idempotent.  Returns GF_OK or GF_ERR_CRYPTO (library too old).
.TP
int \fBgf_random\fP (void *buf, size_t len);
Fill BUF with LEN cryptographically strong random bytes.
.TP
int \fBgf_ct_equal\fP (const void *a, const void *b, size_t n);
Constant\-time comparison of two N\-byte buffers: 1 if equal, else 0. Use for every comparison involving a MAC, tag or secret.
.TP
void \fBgf_wipe\fP (void *secret, size_t len);
Overwrite SECRET with zeros in a way the compiler may not elide.
